WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:03.133
- [Mark] All right, Shiann.

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.530
Shiann, where you from originally?

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:05.363
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.363 --> 00:00:07.270
- [Shiann] Ohio.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:08.740
- [Mark] What part of Ohio?

00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:09.740
- [Shiann] Columbus.

00:00:10.729 --> 00:00:11.860
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.380
Did you have both of your
parents, when you were a kid?

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.560
- No, my parents weren't around that much.

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.882
There was drugs involved.

00:00:20.882 --> 00:00:22.120
- [Mark] You say your
parents were into drugs?

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.617
- [Shiann] Yeah and my parents still are.

00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:25.780
My real dad recently died so,

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.320
when I was 17, I had to
find out the hard way,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.233
but my mom's still around.

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:36.430
Pray to God, I wish she
would just die, but no.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:37.670
Can't wish that on your mother

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.157
when that's the only person you have.

00:00:40.157 --> 00:00:41.607
- [Mark] And how old are you now?

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:42.440
- I'm 20.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:43.930
- [Mark] You're 20.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:46.170
And how long have you
been living on the street?

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:47.260
- Four years.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.206
- [Mark] Four years.

00:00:48.206 --> 00:00:50.213
How was the rest of
your childhood if your,

00:00:50.213 --> 00:00:51.163
your dad passed away when?

00:00:51.163 --> 00:00:53.400
- When I was 17.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.300
My brother had just
turned nine at the time.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.461
- [Mark] How was your childhood?

00:00:57.461 --> 00:00:59.893
- Pretty shitty

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.693
- [Mark] What kind of stuff went on?

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:06.840
- My mom let my family molest me

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.823
so she could get her drugs for free.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:14.653
So I was getting raped by my
family at the age of seven.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.160
I came down here to find out
she was trying to do it again,

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:22.350
so I just volunteered and
started doing it for her.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:25.382
I started selling my body for her so...

00:01:25.382 --> 00:01:26.940
- [Mark] And that's
how you make money now?

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:29.070
- It was. I don't do that anymore.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:30.920
I usually ask for money if I need it.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.290
- [Mark] And people help you out?

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:34.960
- Yeah, sometimes.
Depends on who they are.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.440
If this piece of shit don't
care about anything but drugs,

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.470
then we'll help you out.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.020
- [Mark] So when did you
come to West Virginia?

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.263
- When I turned 18, got out of jail.

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:46.890
I was in Ohio.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:48.872
I got out of jail in Ohio

00:01:48.872 --> 00:01:50.180
and I came down here.

00:01:50.180 --> 00:01:51.806
I got tired of getting in trouble.

00:01:51.806 --> 00:01:54.625
- [Mark] How did you
decide on West Virginia?

00:01:54.625 --> 00:01:56.960
- My mom called me, asked
me to come down here

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:57.930
and I did.

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:58.763
- [Mark] Your mom lives here?

00:01:58.763 --> 00:02:02.270
- Yeah. My mom lives actually
on Locus right up here,

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:05.210
up the road so she's pretty close by,

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:07.810
but just doesn't like
answering the door for me

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:08.963
for some reason.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:11.970
- [Mark] So where do you sleep at night?

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.840
- I usually go to a bando.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.210
- [Mark] What's that? What's a bando?

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.300
- Like abandoned house where nobody lives

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.720
but people like trashed it and left.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:22.553
- [Mark] I see.

00:02:22.553 --> 00:02:25.343
And are drugs a part of your life as well?

00:02:26.730 --> 00:02:27.920
- Yeah.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:29.750
- [Mark] Which drug do you use most often?

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.030
- Heroin. meth, weed.

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:34.822
Anything I can get my hands on honestly.

00:02:34.822 --> 00:02:37.230
- [Mark] Yeah. Does using drugs

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.260
kind of help you forget about
what happened as a child?

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:41.603
- Yeah, I run away from my problems.

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:45.200
People ask me why I do so much,

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.040
'cause I'm running away from my problems.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.100
Running away from my past.

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.660
Helps me forget stuff that happens

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:53.463
or people that pissed
me off during the day.

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.680
Makes me feel good about everything.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.090
Makes me not wanna kill myself.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:02:57.923
Jump off a bridge.

00:02:57.923 --> 00:03:00.310
(indistinct) jumped off
a bridge the other day.

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:02.500
- [Mark] You get suicidal sometimes?

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:04.100
- It's most likely all the time.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:10.673
People spread rumors around
this town that aren't true,

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:15.160
and call somebody that's 20
years old through in life

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:18.380
and has a 20 year old kid
that they walk the street.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.523
I'm never afraid to walk the streets.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:26.120
I had to have five, six people
with me to walk the streets

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:28.790
because people have tried to
come behind me and kill me.

00:03:28.790 --> 00:03:30.420
- [Mark] It's dangerous here?

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:33.350
- Yeah. Very. Like, I prayed to God

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.950
that my brother does not come down here

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.165
when he gets older, that's,

00:03:37.165 --> 00:03:40.897
I don't want to find him dead in a ditch

00:03:40.897 --> 00:03:44.930
from drugs or dead with
a needle out of his arm.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:45.763
That's my brother.

00:03:45.763 --> 00:03:47.320
I looked out for him that I was younger.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:49.440
That's all I had to
growing up was my brother.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.290
We had each other.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:52.193
We wouldn't have parents that cared.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:56.510
About drugs, yeah; about us, no.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.450
- [Mark] So we're in a very
rural part of the country.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:02.150
You can still find drugs like
heroin and crystal meth here?

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:05.920
- Yeah. I am finding them,
but I can find shit like that

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:08.550
better in Salem than I can
here in Clarksburg, honestly.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.670
Clarksburg is so dry
because of coronavirus,

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:12.920
prices went up on everything.

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.790
- [Mark] But you can still find stuff?

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.843
- Yeah, in Salem.

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:20.799
But in Salem, I don't do
anything else other than weed.

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:22.790
I don't fuck with anything else.

00:04:22.790 --> 00:04:23.926
I don't have needles.

00:04:23.926 --> 00:04:26.810
I don't shoot up heroin.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:30.523
Like the dude that I'm
living with, my boyfriend,

00:04:30.523 --> 00:04:34.218
he told me he'd rather see me
with then anybody else here

00:04:34.218 --> 00:04:38.430
while he's in jail, he
doesn't believe heroin.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:40.280
His mom died of heroin.

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:44.140
She OD'd and he found
her and he's only 26.

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:47.670
Like he told her that he
doesn't want to talk to her

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:49.650
because of the fucked up shit she's doing.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:50.583
And she died.

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:53.660
And he didn't get to say
goodbye or anything to her.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.583
Like, I don't know how that shit feels.

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:58.960
I didn't get to say goodbye
to my dad, actually.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.283
So I know how to feels.

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.160
I try to do as much drugs as I can do

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.600
to die, sometimes.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.060
I had to be shocked six time already

00:05:12.060 --> 00:05:16.430
because I OD'd on four buns of heroin.

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:18.733
By myself, I did four buns a day.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:22.463
I did. I don't do that much anymore.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.523
But I did.

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:28.793
- [Mark] What's the hardest part

00:05:28.793 --> 00:05:31.160
of this lifestyle that you're living?

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:32.563
- Drugs, getting by,

00:05:32.563 --> 00:05:35.203
trying to find out where
the next meal comes from.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.240
Where you sleep at, if anybody's
going to try to kill you,

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.700
If people is giving you fake stuff

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:45.300
if people was ratting on
you, wearing a wire on you.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.033
- [Mark] What's the worst thing

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:51.580
that's happened to you out here?

00:05:53.623 --> 00:05:58.623
- I had a hot shot of
insulin, just insulin.

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:02.460
I turned gray, had to be
rushed to the hospital.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.650
- [Mark] A hot shot is where
somebody puts something

00:06:03.650 --> 00:06:06.280
in your drug that you don't know about?

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:10.450
- Yeah, but my hot shot was just insulin.

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:11.443
I'm not diabetic.

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:15.593
So it kind of about killed me.

00:06:16.767 --> 00:06:18.788
- [Mark] And do you have children?

00:06:18.788 --> 00:06:21.763
I have two boys already,

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.840
and one on the way.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:26.673
- [Mark] Oh, you're pregnant.

00:06:26.673 --> 00:06:27.506
- Yeah.

00:06:27.506 --> 00:06:29.120
- [Mark] How far along are you?

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:32.270
- About four months, I guess to say.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:34.010
I don't eat that much.

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:36.463
Like I have really bad eating disorder

00:06:36.463 --> 00:06:40.203
and I get so strung out on dope
like I don't eat that much.

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:46.060
Like I can sit here and do dope right now

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:46.970
and not give two fucks.

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:49.010
Like fuck this, fuck that.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.880
Like if I was thinking about my childhood,

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.123
that's all I care about.

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:54.110
- [Mark] Trying to forget
about your childhood?

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:56.553
Yeah, I run from my
problems, it helps me forget,

00:06:56.553 --> 00:06:59.183
like, if I start thinking of
something from my childhood,

00:06:59.183 --> 00:07:02.323
I do some drug, it helps me.

00:07:02.323 --> 00:07:03.840
Like I forget about what I was thinking.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.590
Like I forgot what I was thinking about.

00:07:05.590 --> 00:07:08.930
And I'd think for hours about
what I was thinking about.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:10.890
Then I finally found out
what I was thinking about

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.060
and I do drugs again.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.363
Forget about it do again.

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:18.780
- [Mark] And who's raising your two kids?

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:20.890
- Their grandparents.

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:23.720
- [Mark] And your third baby on the way

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:26.629
will probably go to them as well?

00:07:26.629 --> 00:07:31.100
- I'm getting ready to go to
40-day detox in Parkersburg.

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:32.250
As soon as I go back to Salem

00:07:32.250 --> 00:07:33.950
and my friends can help me get in.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:38.100
And after that, hopefully,
hopefully I can stay

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.880
through all this detox,
not come home in one day.

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:43.290
- [Mark] Have you tried
to get clean before?

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.980
- I was clean for three
months off shooting

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.068
and then everything else
before I came back to town

00:07:48.068 --> 00:07:51.233
three days ago, I was only doing weed.

00:07:52.722 --> 00:07:56.310
And kind of thought about
something from my past.

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:58.250
And people would bring it up

00:08:02.409 --> 00:08:04.250
kinda got got involved in meth and heroin

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:05.870
and shooting up again.

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:07.703
Like in the last five seconds.

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:13.920
Like when you see a person
put a needle in their arm

00:08:15.030 --> 00:08:17.240
it makes you want to do it so bad.

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:19.040
And I asked that person for a point,

00:08:20.588 --> 00:08:24.690
and I shot myself up
like five or six times

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:29.533
and got to the point where
I didn't know where I was.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:34.690
Like I was lost, I was
shaking, I was crying,

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:36.913
though people were trying to come kill me.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.593
I didn't know where I was.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:44.704
I woke up every night saying
somebody's at the window,

00:08:44.704 --> 00:08:45.950
somebody's throwing stuff out the door.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:47.300
And there was nobody there.

00:08:50.606 --> 00:08:52.056
Like you get to a point where

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:55.847
you see, you go long Wendy's trail,

00:08:55.847 --> 00:09:00.350
you see dead bodies for
people, killed people.

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:04.190
You discover heads in trash bags,

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:05.623
body parts everywhere.

00:09:06.870 --> 00:09:10.370
Find it out a couple months ago

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:15.250
my friend died because
a drug deal gone wrong.

00:09:15.250 --> 00:09:17.990
He wasn't supposed to be at
the place he was at the time,

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.630
and it went all wrong and they killed him.

00:09:19.630 --> 00:09:21.550
And that person that God...

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.420
So yeah, you find dead bodies.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.240
You find points to find heads.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:30.550
You find people with hedged chopped off.

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:32.993
People around my age, dying.

00:09:32.993 --> 00:09:34.340
It's hard.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.206
Especially if you know
the person very well

00:09:36.206 --> 00:09:38.440
your best friend gets shot

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:42.190
by her fricking foster dad

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:44.520
that loves her, that has
a freaking crush on her

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.290
that wants to be with her.

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:49.053
Gets shot, loses life
over something stupid.

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:53.340
Leaves a three-year-old daughter behind

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:57.380
She sees spirits, so she sees her dad

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:59.763
and says, mommy, daddy
said he will be okay.

00:10:01.566 --> 00:10:04.583
You don't see that in typical child.

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:08.980
Typical child doesn't see their dad.

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:18.453
So yeah, this town's fucked up.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.494
I'm actually getting to back to Ohio

00:10:25.494 --> 00:10:27.720
because (indistinct)

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:31.580
and hopefully I can go home
after I go and try, go get help.

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:34.480
My foster parents, hopefully
they'll let me come back home

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.810
because I don't want to
be in this state no more.

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:41.110
I don't want no where near West Virginia.

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:42.450
I don't care where I go

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:44.889
as long as it's far away from here.

00:10:44.889 --> 00:10:48.390
I don't care about going to
prison and some other countries

00:10:48.390 --> 00:10:53.030
as long as it's far away from
here, you know what I mean?

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:54.297
Like this town's fucked up.

00:10:54.297 --> 00:10:56.070
You dead bodies and shit like that.

00:10:56.070 --> 00:10:57.640
You shouldn't have to find that

00:10:57.640 --> 00:11:00.023
on a daily basis because people fuck up.

00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:03.360
People wear wires on people.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:05.053
Then that person finds out.

00:11:06.443 --> 00:11:09.430
You find that person in
the river the next day.

00:11:09.430 --> 00:11:11.460
You won't find him alive.

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:14.210
He's either on a river or on a trail.

00:11:14.210 --> 00:11:17.970
I will not walk along those
trails during the day.

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:20.090
In the morning, at night, I don't care.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:21.850
I hope he will not see me down there

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:25.048
unless I have a good strong muscular man

00:11:25.048 --> 00:11:28.849
that's about this big round with me.

00:11:28.849 --> 00:11:30.490
Somebody with knife,

00:11:30.490 --> 00:11:34.091
a frigging (indistinct) thing,
machete, guns, something.

00:11:34.091 --> 00:11:38.080
Like my friend had to walk
with me all day, one day

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:38.913
the collect drugs

00:11:38.913 --> 00:11:40.160
because I was so scared.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:41.490
And he was the only
person that had a knife.

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:44.697
I don't carry that stuff
with me because cops don't

00:11:44.697 --> 00:11:47.600
really like (indistinct).

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:49.673
If cop pisses me off I start swinging.

00:11:51.887 --> 00:11:53.947
- [Mark] Are their jail and prison times

00:11:53.947 --> 00:11:58.061
that you'll get for conviction
prostitution or drug use?

00:11:58.061 --> 00:12:00.830
- [Shiann] Actually, a
cop has bailed me out

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:02.570
of prostitution nine times

00:12:02.570 --> 00:12:05.180
but that's cause my
boyfriend dosed drugs to him

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:09.600
like the cops around here
buy drugs, honestly, they do.

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:12.110
I've bought, I had chief
of police buy drugs

00:12:12.110 --> 00:12:14.453
from me and my boyfriend like is bad.

00:12:15.526 --> 00:12:19.280
Like they go around
every Thursday at night

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:21.030
at (indistinct) and give CIs,

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:22.723
freaking drugs out of their car.

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:26.530
Like it was bad.

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:27.363
And you see that shit and you're like,

00:12:27.363 --> 00:12:30.483
what the fuck is going
on in this world today?

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:34.343
What the fuck is going on?

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:36.560
You know what I mean?

